          <declname>is224</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function calculates the SHA-224 or SHA-256 checksum of a buffer. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function allocates the context, performs the calculation, and frees the context.</para><para>The SHA-256 result is calculated as output = SHA-256(input buffer).</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>input</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The buffer holding the data. This must be a readable buffer of length <computeroutput>ilen</computeroutput> Bytes. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ilen</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The length of the input data in Bytes. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>output</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The SHA-224 or SHA-256 checksum result. This must be a writable buffer of length <computeroutput>32</computeroutput> bytes for SHA-256, <computeroutput>28</computeroutput> bytes for SHA-224. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>is224</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Determines which function to use. This must be either <computeroutput>0</computeroutput> for SHA-256, or <computeroutput>1</computeroutput> for SHA-224.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>0</computeroutput> on success. </para><simplesectsep/><para>A negative error code on failure. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
